[]},{"id":10831,"date":"2020-07-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Internal Medicine","attending":"Dr. Maria Gonzalez","cc":"Fatigue and lightheadedness during 48-hour religious fast","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5013],"sections":[{"sid":44073,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Fatigue and lightheadedness during 48-hour religious fast"]},{"sid":44074,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns with lightheadedness and fatigue, similar to January 2020 postural episodes, and is participating in a 48-hour religious fast during which he has only consumed water.","He last ate a large meal consisting of rice, lentils, and vegetables before beginning the fast."]},{"sid":44075,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Orthostatic hypotension (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":44076,"type":"medications","lines":["He takes no medications."]},{"sid":44077,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":44078,"type":"family_history","lines":["- No significant family history of cardiovascular disease, syncope, or sudden cardiac death"]},{"sid":44079,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker. Alcohol: None. Occupation: Graduate student."]},{"sid":44080,"type":"vitals","lines":["Vital signs are stable."]},{"sid":44081,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["His physical exam is unremarkable aside from mild orthostatic hypotension."]},{"sid":44082,"type":"labs","lines":["Basic metabolic panel is normal except for a serum glucose of 68 mg/dL."]},{"sid":44083,"type":"assessment","lines":["The liver is primarily responsible for maintaining his blood glucose at this stage of fasting.","Hormonal signaling has triggered a shift in hepatic enzyme activity through changes in phosphorylation status."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10832,"date":"2021-07-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Internal Medicine","attending":"Dr. James O'Brien","cc":"Fatigue and 2-3 pound weight loss after 3-day hiking trip with limited food intake","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4959],"sections":[{"sid":44084,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Fatigue and 2-3 pound weight loss after 3-day hiking trip with limited food intake"]},{"sid":44085,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns with recurrent fasting-related fatigue, having presented in July 2020 with similar symptoms during a 48-hour religious fast.","He is participating in a three-day hiking trip through a remote national park.","Due to limited supplies, he has consumed only small amounts of jerky and water over the past two days.","He reports feeling tired but mentally alert.","He has lost about 2\u20133 pounds during the trip but denies nausea, vomiting, or abdominal pain.","He last urinated several hours ago and notes that it was dark yellow."]},{"sid":44086,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Orthostatic hypotension (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Starvation (diagnosed 2020-07-15)"]},{"sid":44087,"type":"medications","lines":["He takes no medications"]},{"sid":44088,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":44089,"type":"family_history","lines":["- No significant family history of cardiovascular disease, syncope, or sudden cardiac death"]},{"sid":44090,"type":"social_history","lines":["He denies alcohol or drug use"]},{"sid":44091,"type":"vitals","lines":["His vital signs are within normal limits"]},{"sid":44092,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Physical exam shows a lean but well-hydrated man with no jaundice or hepatosplenomegaly"]},{"sid":44093,"type":"assessment","lines":["While sitting by the campfire, he and a friend discuss how the body adapts to fasting, especially the metabolic shift in the liver during prolonged periods without food.","In the fasting state, glucagon levels rise and insulin levels fall.","This hormonal environment favors hepatic glucose production to maintain euglycemia.","Glucagon acts by activating protein kinase A (PKA), which phosphorylates key liver enzymes.","In contrast to insulin, which promotes dephosphorylation, glucagon-induced phosphorylation favors enzymes that drive gluconeogenesis and glycogenolysis while suppressing glycolysis and glycogenesis.","These phosphorylation changes occur within minutes and are a primary regulatory mechanism during fasting."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10833,"date":"2022-07-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Aisha Johnson","cc":"Collapse immediately following 10-kilometer race with dizziness and lightheadedness","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[964],"sections":[{"sid":44094,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Collapse immediately following 10-kilometer race with dizziness and lightheadedness"]},{"sid":44095,"type":"hpi","lines":["He returns with similar lightheadedness, having experienced postural symptoms in 2020 and fasting-related episodes in 2020 and 2021.","He reports feeling dizzy and lightheaded upon finishing the race but denies any loss of consciousness.","He is well-hydrated and has been training for several months.","His symptoms resolve with lying down and leg elevation."]},{"sid":44096,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Orthostatic hypotension (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Starvation (diagnosed 2020-07-15)","- Fasting metabolic state with PKA activation (diagnosed 2021-07-15)"]},{"sid":44097,"type":"allergies","lines":["He has no known drug allergies"]},{"sid":44098,"type":"family_history","lines":["- No significant family history of cardiovascular disease, syncope, or sudden cardiac death"]},{"sid":44099,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker. Alcohol: None. Occupation: Graduate student."]},{"sid":44100,"type":"vitals","lines":["On examination, his blood pressure is 90/60 mmHg, heart rate is 58 beats per minute, and he is afebrile."]},{"sid":44101,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["His skin is cool and moist, and his capillary refill time is less than 2 seconds.","His cardiovascular examination is normal with no murmurs, rubs, or gallops.","His lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.","The remainder of the p